  "body": "## What changed\n\nA 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive or 2D Offset with the stock as its source built its region from the whole stock footprint. The cut went through the parts of the setup, and generate said `ok`. Only the keep law (#1603, PR #1615) found the gouge after generate.\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/area.rs`: new `stock_pocket`. For a pocket family op with `SrcRef::Stock`, the region is the stock footprint minus the parts that stand in the step-down ladder. This is the same island law as the whole-model pocket (#12). A tilted frame uses the local facets.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/job.rs`: `collect_job` calls `stock_pocket` for a stock source before the generic region build.\n- When no part stands in the ladder, the function returns nothing and the region is the stock footprint as before. Thus no golden changes.\n- When the parts fill the whole stock outline, generate refuses: \"a pocket on the stock clears the stock around the setup's parts, and the parts fill the whole stock outline at Z ... - pick the area to clear, or use the model as the source\".\n- An area offset into the part still gouges. The keep law still refuses the post for it.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1554-stock-source-around-part.md`.\n\nThe second \"Done means\" line of the issue (a 2D Adaptive on a model source skips an outside band narrower than the tool, with no note) moves to #1655. A note there can change CL goldens, so it is a separate issue.\n\n## Readings and pinning tests\n\n`crates/app/tests/keep_law.rs`:\n\n- `a_stock_source_clearing_goes_around_the_part_and_posts` (new pin): 2D Pocket 20 to 5 and 2D Adaptive 20 to 10, on an aligned and on a turned stock. No blocking warning, no feed move over the part, and the program posts.\n  - Without the `job.rs` arm, the test fails (19 `Gouge` warnings on 2D Pocket, stock not turned). With the fix, it passes.\n- `a_stock_source_area_offset_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`: an offset of +3 still gouges, and the post is refused (the backstop stays).\n- `over_mcp_the_pocket_family_keeps_the_part_the_same`: over MCP, a stock source now gives 0 gouges and verify is ok. A stock source with offset 3.0 gouges and verify is not ok.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` on head 2c049d69d: ok, 18 app binaries (lib + 17 suites) in 281 s, 0 failed.\n- More suites that have stock-source pocket ops, all pass: area_open, area_picks, carried_fixture_shape, contour_start_point, corner_blend, engrave_law, golden_cl, heights, heights_selection, ladder_entry_height, lead_approach, level_links, machine_switch, mill2d_b, operations, pick_doors, post_not_judged, probe_op, program_comments, project_roundtrip, roughing2d, setup_post_options, sinker_electrode, solid_law_goldens, stock_source_verdict, tilt, tool_gate, trochoid_law.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A tilted (3+2) frame with a stock source. The code path uses the local facets, but no test covers it.\n- A stock made from the model. The UI. The release heavy lanes.\n- Known limit: the islands are the union over all ladder planes (as in #12). Levels above the part top keep stock over the part, so they do not cut it.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive or 2D Offset with the stock as its source now clears the stock around the setup's parts, and does not cut through them (#1554)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1554\n",
